  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tiger, prey and detailed threat surveys in Thung Yai Wildlife Sanctuaries to inform tiger conservation interventions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this grant is to obtain an understanding of tiger population trends in Thung Yai East Wildlife Sanctuary (TYE) and Thung Yai West (TYW) and the impact upon those trends of threats emanating from seven villages in TYE so that appropriate management actions may be developed. Specifically the Recipient will: (1) conduct a camera trap survey in TYE using about 50 camera trap points at 4-5 kilometers spacing, placed in two blocks of 25 trapping points per block and conducted over a 2 month period; (2) conduct a similar camera trap survey in TYW; and (3) undertake a rigorous analysis of the threats emanating from the seven villages that are found in the northwestern valley that runs through TYE by recording data in three areas on human activities, sign of target wildlife species, livestock grazing, tiger predation, location of poaching, poaching patterns.</narrative>
  </description>
